+    * one of ``stranded``: its own change does not merge onto ``<base_remote>/<base>``, tried
+      after what its branch was built on (the base moved since it was cut), and ``name``,
+      built on the base, carries what it clashes with. Its branch is to be rebuilt on the
+      new base; ``name`` is not blamed, nor told to change.
+    * a prerequisite ``name`` declares (``Depends on`` / ``Depends on (merged)`` / ``Stacks
+      on``) whose work its branch does not hold: ``name``'s branch is to be rebuilt on it.
+      No ``Conflicts with`` is proposed: the edge is there already.
+    * any other: the ``Conflicts with`` proposal a same-wave hold gets (``_CONFLICT_STEP``,
+      #674). No brief is written."""
