+    plus ``kept`` conflicts with something else the line took in after ``pre`` — the base,
+    merged in for a bundle of the wave whose PR merged and whose branch is gone
+    (:func:`_take_in_base`). Neither is a conflict with the bundles kept, so none of them
+    is named; the fold then judges it against every bundle on the line
+    (:func:`_held_on_line`, #739), and stops on it when that holds nothing. ``partners``:
+    each bundle of ``kept`` tried on its own (``pre``, then it, then ``head``) that
+    ``head`` conflicts with; when it conflicts only with several of them together, all of
+    them. ``paths``: the files left conflicting on ``pre`` plus ``kept``. The trials never
